{
  "description": "A quadrupedal creature is shown in right-facing side profile standing on a small patch of sandy, pebbly ground against a plain off-white background. The overall body shape, head, neck, legs and tail are horse-like and covered in short to medium-length brown fur, but the central trunk region is covered in scaly, bumpy skin unlike fur. The fur is dark brown on the head, neck, shoulders, hindquarters and legs, with a long hairy tail hanging from the rear. The mid-back and sides are covered by a dark mottled gray-blue scaly area with irregular spots and a slightly raised bumpy ridge along the spine, bordered below by a wavy edge lined with small white nodules where it meets the fur. The lower side and belly are pale off-white to light gray with numerous scattered raised white tubercles. The head has an elongated muzzle, visible nostril, dark eye, and mouth with whiskers at the lip, and the neck bears a short, bristly brown mane along its dorsal edge.",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "head",
      "looks_like": "elongated horse-like head with brown fur, a dark eye with eyelid, a large nostril on the muzzle, a closed mouth with short whiskers at the lower lip and chin, and a slightly lighter tan around the muzzle",
      "where": "at the anterior end of the neck, facing to the right"
    },
    {
      "part": "ears",
      "looks_like": "two upright, pointed, fur-covered ears with darker inner edges",
      "where": "on top of the head, one slightly behind the other in side view"
    },
    {
      "part": "mane",
      "looks_like": "short, bristly, dark brown hair forming a ridge",
      "where": "along the dorsal midline of the neck from just behind the ears to where the scaly back begins"
    },
    {
      "part": "legs",
      "looks_like": "four sturdy, columnar legs covered in brown fur that is longer and shaggier on the upper portions and shorter and darker near the joints, with visible knee/hock joints",
      "where": "two forelegs under the chest/shoulder and two hindlegs under the hindquarters, supporting the body ventrally"
    },
    {
      "part": "feet",
      "looks_like": "rounded, solid hooves, light gray-brown with a slightly worn texture, broader at the base",
      "where": "at the distal tip of each of the four legs, in contact with the ground"
    },
    {
      "part": "tail",
      "looks_like": "long, thick, straight hair tail, brown with individual strands visible, hanging vertically with slight flare at the bottom",
      "where": "extending from the posterior end of the body at the rump, reaching to near the level of the hocks"
    },
    {
      "part": "scales",
      "looks_like": "small, bumpy, overlapping scaly skin with raised tubercles and scattered circular spots; dark mottled gray-blue to blackish on the dorsal saddle and pale whitish-gray with many small white raised nodules on the ventral belly and lower side; the border between fur and scales is wavy and lined with a row of white bead-like bumps",
      "where": "covering the central trunk: the dorsal saddle from behind the shoulders across the back to the base of the tail, and the lateral and ventral belly between the fore and hind legs"
    },
    {
      "part": "markings",
      "looks_like": "color pattern of solid brown fur on head, neck, shoulders, hindquarters and legs contrasted with a dark mottled scaly dorsal patch and a pale ventral belly densely dotted with white tubercles; the transition line between fur and scales is distinct and undulating",
      "where": "across the entire body, with brown fur anteriorly and posteriorly and scaly pattern centrally"
    }
  ],
  "attached_objects": [],
  "animals": ["horse", "fish"],
  "separate_bodies": 1,
  "heads": 1,
  "walking_legs": 4,
  "wings": 0,
  "extra_limb_pieces": 0,
  "tails": 1
}
